        "response": {
          "output": "Add the flagged keys to `confirmed-typos` in the Akka Diagnostics checker config. I couldn't search this repo to confirm, so this comes from my knowledge of Akka Diagnostics.\n\n```hocon\nakka.diagnostics.checker {\n  # Keys the checker should treat as intentional, not as typos\n  confirmed-typos = [\n    \"akka.my-custom.setting-name\",\n  ]\n\n  # Or silence a whole check by name (the warning text shows the check name)\n  # disabled-checks = [\"typo\"]\n}\n```\n\nUse the full key path exactly as the warning prints it. If the flagged keys are your own app settings under `akka.*`, move them to your own namespace (e.g. `my-app.*`). The typo check only looks at `akka.*` keys, so it will then stop flagging them.\n\nIf you're using a different checker than Akka Diagnostics, tell me which one and I'll look at its config."
