        "prompt": {
          "raw": "You are a helpful senior engineer. Answer the request directly and concretely.\n\nUser request:\nThe logs say something about thread starvation. What is that telling me?",
          "label": "evals/akka-diagnostics/prompt-baseline.txt: You are a helpful senior engineer. Answer the request directly and concretely.\n\nUser request:\n{{request}}",
          "config": {}
        },
        "promptId": "00a83e7e1b4aa396265c545e5a1e7a7b582a4bc074e8af9734ee6017ba71f2de",
        "promptIdx": 0,
        "provider": {
          "id": "exec:../_provider/claude.sh",
          "label": "sonnet-baseline"
        },
        "response": {
          "output": "It means a dispatcher's threads were all busy or blocked. Akka Diagnostics' starvation detector schedules a trivial task on the dispatcher, and that task waited longer than `max-delay-warning-threshold` (default 100ms) to run.\n\nThe usual cause is blocking work on the default dispatcher: JDBC, sync HTTP, `Await.result`, `Thread.sleep`, or heavy CPU work. While threads are stuck, actors can't process messages and `Future` callbacks wait. You see latency and timeouts with low CPU. Cluster heartbeats can be delayed too, which can cause false unreachable or quarantine events.\n\nWhat to do:\n1. **Read the stack traces in the warning.** They show what the busy threads are doing. Trust them over thread-state counts, because native blocking IO shows as `RUNNABLE`. One warning is one sample, so check that several point at the same call.\n2. **Move that blocking call to a dedicated dispatcher.** Use a `thread-pool-executor` dispatcher and run the work there.\n3. **Don't raise the threshold or enlarge the default dispatcher.** That hides the problem.\n\nIf the warning names a dispatcher other than the default, the same logic applies to that dispatcher. If you paste the warning and its traces, I can point at the specific culprit."
        },
        "score": 1,
        "success": true,
        "testCase": {
          "description": "starvation",
          "vars": {
            "request": "file:///private/tmp/b6/evals/akka-diagnostics/cases/starvation.txt"
          },
          "assert": [
            {
              "type": "javascript",
              "metric": "accuracy",
              "value": "if (!/starvation|blocking|dispatcher|thread pool|blocked/i.test(output)) throw new Error('explains the thread starvation detector');\nreturn true;\n"
            }
          ],
          "options": {},
          "metadata": {}
        },
